---
interface TutorialStep {
	readonly title: string;
	readonly body: string;
	readonly href?: string;
	readonly label?: string;
}

interface HowToGuide {
	readonly title: string;
	readonly text: string;
	readonly links: ReadonlyArray<{ readonly href: string; readonly label: string }>;
}

interface ReferenceSection {
	readonly label: string;
	readonly items: ReadonlyArray<readonly [string, string]>;
}

interface Props {
	bannerSrc?: string;
	isLandscape?: boolean;
	tutorialSteps: ReadonlyArray<TutorialStep>;
	howToGuides: ReadonlyArray<HowToGuide>;
	referenceSections?: ReadonlyArray<ReferenceSection>;
}

const {
	bannerSrc,
	isLandscape = false,
	tutorialSteps,
	howToGuides,
	referenceSections = [],
} = Astro.props as Props;
---

<div class="guide">
	<div class="hero">
		<p class="hero-tagline">Learn the forecast before you change the weather</p>
	</div>

	<p class="lead">
		This guide is the fastest way to onboard into <strong>Płanetnik</strong> and understand how to use the reports in a
		practical sequence.
	</p>

	<p>
		It follows the <strong><a href="https://diataxis.fr/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Diátaxis</a></strong> model so that help is easier to use: start with a tutorial, move into
		task-focused how-to guidance, use the reference map when you need to locate information quickly, and read the
		explanation sections when you want the reasoning behind the product.
	</p>

	{bannerSrc && (
		<div class="section-banner">
			<img src={bannerSrc} alt="Planetnik guide banner" class="section-banner-image" />
		</div>
	)}

	<hr />

	<h3>Tutorials</h3>
	<p>Use these when you are new to Płanetnik and want a guided path instead of a menu of unrelated reports.</p>

	<div class="guide-grid">
		{tutorialSteps.map((step, index) => (
			<article class="guide-card">
				<div class="guide-card-kicker">tutorial {index + 1}</div>
				<h4>{step.title}</h4>
				<p>{step.body}</p>
				{step.href && step.label && (
					<a href={step.href} class="guide-link">{step.label}</a>
				)}
			</article>
		))}
	</div>

	<blockquote>
		{isLandscape
			? "Recommended first pass: landscape dashboard → repositories → pick a repo → hotspots → contributors."
			: "Recommended first pass: reports → open a report → hotspots → dependencies → contributors → controls."}
	</blockquote>

	<hr />

	<h3>How-To Guides</h3>
	<p>Use these when you already know what you are trying to accomplish and need the shortest route to the right view.</p>

	<div class="guide-grid">
		{howToGuides.map((guide) => (
			<article class="guide-card">
				<h4>{guide.title}</h4>
				<p>{guide.text}</p>
				{guide.links.length > 0 && (
					<ul class="link-list">
						{guide.links.map((link) => (
							<li><a href={link.href}>{link.label}</a></li>
						))}
					</ul>
				)}
			</article>
		))}
	</div>

	{referenceSections.length > 0 && (
		<>
			<hr />
			<h3>Reference</h3>
			<p>Use this section when you know the name of a report area and want a quick description of what each page contains.</p>
			<div class="reference-grid">
				{referenceSections.map((section) => (
					<section class="reference-card">
						<h4>{section.label}</h4>
						<dl>
							{section.items.map(([href, text]) => (
								<>
									<dt><a href={href}>{href}</a></dt>
									<dd>{text}</dd>
								</>
							))}
						</dl>
					</section>
				))}
			</div>
		</>
	)}

	<hr />

	<h3>Explanation</h3>
	<p>Use these notes when you want to understand why the reports are organized the way they are and how to interpret them together.</p>

	{isLandscape ? (
		<>
			<h4>Start From the Landscape, Then Drill Down</h4>
			<p>
				The landscape dashboard gives you the organisation-wide view. When something stands out (size, contributor concentration,
				tag patterns) drill into the specific repository to investigate with the full single-repo analysis.
			</p>

			<h4>Read People and Code Together</h4>
			<p>
				Many delivery problems are socio-technical. Use Contributors and Team Topology to understand knowledge spread, coordination
				risk, and ownership concentration across the organisation.
			</p>

			<h4>Use Repository-Level Views for Evidence</h4>
			<p>
				Landscape views show the big picture. When you need evidence for a specific change, drill into a repository
				to access its hotspots, components, file metrics, and quality controls.
			</p>
		</>
	) : (
		<>
			<h4>Start With Queues, Not Charts</h4>
			<p>
				Płanetnik contains many charts, but the product is most useful when it helps you choose a better engineering action.
				That is why Impact, Hotspots, Goals &amp; Controls, and Findings should usually anchor triage.
			</p>

			<h4>Use Multiple Views to Validate a Story</h4>
			<p>
				A single metric is rarely enough. A file is more interesting when it is large <em>and</em> frequently changed.
				A component is more important when it is central <em>and</em> weakly owned. Use structure, history, and people
				views together.
			</p>

			<h4>Read People and Code Together</h4>
			<p>
				Many delivery problems are socio-technical. Use Contributors and Team Topology alongside code-level reports to understand knowledge spread, coordination
				risk, and ownership concentration.
			</p>

			<h4>Prefer Evidence Before Refactoring</h4>
			<p>
				Use Dependencies, Temporal Dependencies, and Duplication to build evidence for change. Refactoring is easier to defend when you can
				show structural pressure, not just discomfort.
			</p>

			<h4>Treat Balanced Coupling as a Pressure Map</h4>
			<p>
				Use Balanced Coupling when you want one page that blends static dependencies, co-change,
				coordination, and knowledge exposure. It is a triage surface, not a replacement for the underlying evidence views.
			</p>
		</>
	)}
</div>

<style>
	.guide {
		max-width: none;
	}

	.guide > :not(.section-banner):not(.guide-grid):not(.reference-grid) {
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.hero {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
		max-width: 720px;
	}

	.hero-tagline {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.lead {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	p {
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	hr {
		border: none;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	h3 {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	h4 {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		margin-top: 0;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	a {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		text-decoration: none;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	blockquote {
		border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
		padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
		margin: 1rem 0;
		font-style: italic;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
		background: var(--color-accent-soft, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.04));
		border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0;
	}

	.guide-grid,
	.reference-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
		margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
	}

	.guide-card,
	.reference-card {
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 18px;
		background: var(--color-card);
		padding: 1.2rem 1.2rem 1.1rem;
	}

	.guide-card p,
	.reference-card p,
	.reference-card dd {
		margin-bottom: 0;
		color: var(--color-text-muted);
	}

	.guide-card-kicker {
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		color: var(--color-accent);
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}

	.guide-link {
		display: inline-flex;
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
	}

	.link-list {
		margin: 0.85rem 0 0 1rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.reference-card dl {
		margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
	}

	.reference-card dt {
		margin-top: 0.8rem;
		font-family: "SF Mono", "Fira Code", monospace;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}

	.reference-card dt:first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.reference-card dd {
		margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.section-banner {
		width: 100%;
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0.5rem;
	}

	.section-banner-image {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 8px;
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.guide-grid,
		.reference-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
